    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Aquatic biogeochemistry",
    "problem": "Existing estimates of methane emissions from lakes are uncertain because they use simplistic upscaling methods that neglect the crucial role of eutrophication, which is expected to increase significantly due to climate change and population growth, thereby accelerating future warming.",
    "method": "This study simulates future methane emissions from lakes and impoundments by applying projected nutrient loading scenarios to a global distribution of lake productivity and using statistical models to predict the resulting changes in methane flux.",
    "task": "The task is to simulate how future eutrophication of global lakes and impoundments, driven by increased nutrient loading, will affect their methane (CH4) emissions throughout the 21st century.",
